  "verdict": "topic << style: at every tested K (20, 30, 50), LDA topic-proportion Ridge LOSO-CV R2 is at or below zero (K=20: -0.545, K=30: -0.004, K=50: -2.943), versus the embedding baseline's stable, clearly-positive R2=0.21 (95% CI [0.03, 0.35], excludes zero). The best-behaved K (K=30, R2=-0.004) is statistically indistinguishable from its own permutation null (-0.037), i.e. no reliable topic-ideology signal survives this probe at any tested K. K=20 and K=50 are further dragged strongly negative (below their own permutation nulls) by LOSO extrapolation instability on one outlier show ('The Moment with Jorge Ramos and Paola Ramos', see loso_outlier_diagnostic per K) -- consistent across all three K, so it reflects that show's topic-distribution being atypical (plausibly its bilingual Spanish/English content skewing far from the mostly-English corpus vocabulary) rather than randomness. Net: ideology in this corpus is carried far more by HOW shows talk (embedding, R2=0.21) than by WHAT they talk about at these topic granularities (LDA, R2<=0). This is a clean, honest 'topic << style' result -- worth a look at whether finer/coarser K or a collinearity-aware feature transform (e.g. CLR) recovers more signal before concluding CA isn't worth building, but the minimal-arm verdict as specified is unambiguous.",
